AB  - The need to uncover the bibliographic field of work-integrated learnin
g (WIL) stems from the increased interest to include WIL in higher edu
cation and present positive outcomes of WIL. This bibliographic review
 of WIL aims to understand the connectedness and trajectory of WIL in 
scientific publications and to explore the most influential actors. Th
e amount of WIL research is increasing rapidly and there is global int
erest in the research field, even if there are dominating countries, s
uch as Australia. From both citations, co-citations, and bibliographic
 coupling it is evident that there are highly influential countries, s
ources, publications, and authors in WIL research, which shape the bib
liographic landscape of WIL. As WIL is an emerging research field, add
itional bibliographic reviews in coming years can show future trends i
n WIL research and potential differences between countries and discipl
ines. 
