AB  - The digital era and online education offers new possibilities for dist
ributing higher education to non-traditional students, for instance fu
ll-working participants. This article describes experiences based on s
ix years’ experience from an online course designed for non-traditiona
l students. An on-line course in statistics, designed for attracting n
on-traditional students is used as a case. It is shown that the charac
teristics of the participants are completely different in comparison t
o traditional campus students. These differences may be rewarding for 
teachers and may offer interesting pedagogical opportunities. 
