AB  - This study builds a market-focused resource-based view (RBV) framework
 on green product innovation (GPI) to examine the relationship between
 market responsiveness, GPI, product advantages, and new product perfo
rmance, as well as the role of industry clockspeed. We adopt a partial
 least squares method to test these relationships using data from 325 
Chinese manufacturing firms. The results show that market responsivene
ss positively affects GPI, and GPI can promote new product performance
 through enhancing product radicalness and meaningfulness. Besides, th
e mediating effect of product meaningfulness is stronger in high- than
 in low-clockspeed industries, while the mediating effect of product r
adicalness does not present a differentiated extent between high- and 
low-clockspeed industries. This study offers a market-focused RBV fram
ework on GPI, illustrates the importance of responsiveness to market i
ntelligence when implementing GPI, and highlights the necessity of inv
estigating additional outcomes of GPI other than aggregated performanc
e measures and comparing these effects among different industries. 
