AB  - An Information Systems Design Theory is a prescriptive theory that off
ers theory-based principles, which can guide practitioners and scholar
s in the design of effective information systems and set an agenda for
 on-going research. This paper introduces and describes an ISDT for ad
aptable E-Learning. We formulate our ISDT based on two cycles of Actio
n Design Research. The cycles were conducted in an authentic organizat
ional setting with end-users, responsible for organizing, producing an
d distributing civic orientation. Based on our findings, we propose th
at our ISDT, together with its components, can be used to design, impl
ement and support an information system that incorporates E-Learning, 
which is not explicitly constrained to the formal context of higher ed
ucation. Â© 2016 IEEE. 
