AB  - The outbreak of the global pandemic COVID-19 meant an extreme intensif
ication of digitalization in education. Around the world, technology b
ecame a prerequisite for continuing education, as schools were to swit
ch to distance education. Drawing on an institutional logics perspecti
ve, this paper aims to explore school leaders' experiences and insight
s from running a virtual school overnight. Data includes a survey of10
5 school leaders in Swedish high schools. The results show clear chall
enges for schools as institutions, yet most of the school leaders perc
eived that the shift to virtual classrooms went well and can lead to l
asting value for the school. Still, when facing a new situation, organ
izational problems are uncovered, and the importance of brick-and-mort
ar schools becomes visible. Contributions include analyzing an extreme
 case of digitization in schools and conceptualizing two faces of digi
talization, that constitute both a preservative and disruptive force i
n institutional logic. 
