AB  - This article is a pilot study on the relationship between performance 
in online classes and behavior in online discussion forums. Measuring 
student activity on the discussion forum, the collected data is then a
nalyzed and mapped to the performance of the students on the course. T
he student activity was dividedinto a number of parameters, and during
 the study these parameters were compared to the performance of the st
udents.The significance of each parameter was also analyzed through a 
Kruskall-Wallis-test Overall there was a strong tendency thatstudents 
with more activity and engagement received higher grades. This is in t
he future useful for developing some kind of monitoring to identify an
d support students on the verge of failing the course. 
