AB  - In order to achieve learning, presence is necessary. If we have good p
resence, no tests are necessary. In distance learning, the concept of 
presence is not obvious. Presence in distance and network contexts usu
ally means being active on social media. However, in distance and netw
ork learning, something more is needed. It is the face-to-face interac
tion that needs to be “digitalized”. In order to investigate this, we 
have turned to Heidegger (1927) and the concept of Dasein. The need fo
r an artifact mediating Dasein has been identified. The concept of Das
ein is not easy, not even in philosophical terms. It means being somew
here else, and not on the place you are present. We have extended the 
The Community of Inquiry Model originating from Garrisson &amp; Anders
son (2003) by introducing the concept of digital Dasein. 
