AB  - Poverty, war, conflicts, and other forces of global turmoil are consta
ntly challenging how developed nations design their processes for immi
gration in general, and civic orientation in particular. This paper fo
cuses on an exploratory study of the challenges coupled with the digit
alization of civic orientation in a region of West Sweden – and conclu
des with a set of five tentative design guidelines for how to design f
or heterogeneous groups of end-users. 
